{"styles":[{"sc":"#ff2600","so":1,"w":2,"ol":true,"fc":"#fffb00","fo":0.502}],"cards":["<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#222222;max-width:238px;\"><div style=\"background:#0e7d46;height:6px;border-radius:3px 3px 0 0;\"></div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:7px 0 0;\">COUNTY BOUNDARY</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:0 0 2px;\">GEORGIA</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-weight:800;padding:2px 0 6px;\">Muscogee County</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;\"><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Population</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">201,830 (2024 est.)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">County Seat</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">Columbus</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Land Area</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">216 sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Density</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">934 / sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Household Income</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$57,010</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Home Value</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$219,700</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#333333;padding:8px 0 2px;border-top:1px solid #eef2f1;margin-top:7px;\">Muscogee County is Georgia's only fully consolidated city-county government, with Columbus's downtown riverfront core, historic districts, and suburban rings all governed as a single jurisdiction along the Chattahoochee River and the Alabama state line. The economy centers on Fort Moore (formerly Fort Benning) just south of the city — one of the Army's largest installations and a major driver of regional employment and rental housing demand — alongside homegrown employers Aflac and Synovus/TSYS headquartered downtown. Columbus State University and a revitalized Uptown/riverfront district, anchored by the Chattahoochee RiverWalk and whitewater course, have spurred infill mixed-use and multifamily development near downtown, while the county's northern side carries its higher-end residential submarkets. Incomes and home values sit below state and metro averages, reflecting a market shaped more by steady military-driven housing turnover than by high-growth suburban expansion.</div><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888888;padding-top:6px;\">Source: U.S. Census Bureau · Data verified: September 13, 2026</div></div>"],"feats":[["Muscogee County",0,[[32.51664,-85.00343],[32.51705,-85.00396],[32.51772,-85.00505],[32.51849,-85.00638],[32.52008,-85.00668],[32.52123,-85.0066],[32.52241,-85.00648],[32.52387,-85.0071],[32.52488,-85.0084],[32.52544,-85.01024],[32.52593,-85.0122],[32.52611,-85.01379],[32.52657,-85.01441],[32.52843,-85.01581],[32.52923,-85.01547],[32.53014,-85.01488],[32.53111,-85.01526],[32.53142,-85.01565],[32.53185,-85.01632],[32.53352,-85.01817],[32.5344,-85.01852],[32.5346,-85.01904],[32.53475,-85.02024],[32.53585,-85.02088],[32.53755,-85.0212],[32.54004,-85.02205],[32.54083,-85.02205],[32.54136,-85.02139],[32.54196,-85.02096],[32.54276,-85.0208],[32.54308,-85.02131],[32.54292,-85.02251],[32.54295,-85.02365],[32.54356,-85.02448],[32.54446,-85.02553],[32.54484,-85.02619],[32.54452,-85.0303],[32.54417,-85.03139],[32.54484,-85.03203],[32.5459,-85.0327],[32.54695,-85.03304],[32.54945,-85.03308],[32.55073,-85.03341],[32.55089,-85.03347],[32.55169,-85.03393],[32.55217,-85.03494],[32.55326,-85.03518],[32.55396,-85.03573],[32.55441,-85.03664],[32.55441,-85.03816],[32.55508,-85.03829],[32.55582,-8